nilla Bean Paste","baseAmount":1,"usUnit":"tbsp","metricAmount":15,"metricUnit":"ml","pantryKey":"vanilla","stepRef":2},{"id":"m53279_12","name":"Unsalted Butter","baseAmount":1.11,"usUnit":"cup","metricAmount":250,"metricUnit":"g","pantryKey":"butter","stepRef":2},{"id":"m53279_13","name":"Filo Pastry","baseAmount":2.22,"usUnit":"cup","metricAmount":500,"metricUnit":"g","pantryKey":"flour","stepRef":2},{"id":"m53279_14","name":"Ground Pistachios","baseAmount":6.7,"usUnit":"tbsp","metricAmount":100,"metricUnit":"g","pantryKey":"pistachio","stepRef":2}]}],"steps":[{"stepNumber":1,"phaseLabel":"Prep & Mix","title":"Melt & Whisk Smooth","instructionTemplate":"First, make the syrup. Tip the sugar into a large saucepan with 650ml water. Stir over a low heat until the sugar has dissolved, then turn up the heat and bring to the boil. Reduce the heat to a simmer and cook for 15 mins, then squeeze in a few drops of lemon juice and simmer for a further 5 mins. Remove from the heat and leave to cool. Meanwhile, for assembling the baklava later, melt the butter in a small pan over a low heat for 5 mins, skimming and discarding any froth that rises to the surface. Incorporate {m53279_1}, {m53279_2}, {m53279_3}, and {m53279_4} smoothly until evenly distributed.","durationMin":3,"timerSeconds":180,"activeMeasureSummary":"Sugar, Lemon Juice","creatorSecret":"Prep and measure sugar first—mise en place makes this dessert twice as fast."},{"stepNumber":2,"phaseLabel":"Build Flavor","title":"Fold In Flavorings & Mix-Ins","instructionTemplate":"For the filling, crush all of the nuts in a pestle and mortar, or blitz in a food processor – you want a mixture of finely ground nuts with a few chunky pieces. Tip into a bowl, stir through the spices and set aside. Incorporate {m53279_5}, {m53279_6}, {m53279_7}, {m53279_8}, {m53279_9}, {m53279_10}, {m53279_11}, {m53279_12}, {m53279_13}, and {m53279_14} smoothly until evenly distributed.","durationMin":3,"timerSeconds":180,"activeMeasureSummary":"Walnuts, Pecan Nuts"},{"stepNumber":3,"phaseLabel":"Shape & Layer","title":"Shape & Press Dough Evenly","instructionTemplate":"$18","durationMin":3,"timerSeconds":180,"activeMeasureSummary":"Almonds, Ground Cinnamon"},{"stepNumber":4,"phaseLabel":"Bake / Chill","title":"Bake Until Golden & Set","instructionTemplate":"Brush with the remaining melted butter. Bake for 20-25 mins until evenly golden, turning the tray around halfway through. While still hot, immediately pour over 5-6 ladlefuls of the syrup. You should hear the syrup sizzle as it hits the hot baklava. Set aside to cool and absorb.","durationMin":3,"timerSeconds":180,"activeMeasureSummary":"Ground Cardomom, Ricotta"},{"stepNumber":5,"phaseLabel":"Viral Finish","title":"Melt & Whisk Smooth","instructionTemplate":"Melt the dark chocolate in a heatproof bowl set over a pan of simmering water, ensuring the bowl doesn’t touch the water, or in the microwave in short bursts. Drizzle this over the cooled baklava and sprinkle with the ground pistachios.","durationMin":30,"timerSeconds":1800,"activeMeasureSummary":"Lemon, Orange","criticalTip":"Let set for 5–10 minutes before slicing or plating so the textures hold crisp and photogenic!","creatorSecret":"Add a pinch of flaky sea salt right as it leaves the oven—it makes the dark chocolate flavor taste 2x richer."}],"ugcQuotes":[{"id":"muq-53279","handle":"@baker_baklava-","image":"./ai-images/baklava-with-spiced-nuts-ricotta-chocolate.jpg","quote":"Followed the scaled metric steps—came out flawless in 45 mins!","rating":5}]}}]
